# These files are round-trip fixtures: the whole point of this corpus is
# that the bytes committed here are the bytes measured against. Line-ending
# normalization would silently rewrite handwritten-simple.sce (a CRLF file as
# found) on checkout under an autocrlf configuration that differs from the
# one used to add it, making the committed fixture no longer the file that
# was actually tested. None of them are touched by anything but the tests
# that read them, so "text" here has no upside and a real downside.
*.sce -text
